<<~ ahu slot=`#/body`>>

Lane tag-burn (road M6, the version burn): every domain-separation signing tag and HKDF info names itself without a version (`lar-<name>`, `lares/<name>`, `lar:<name>`), one commit per tag family with its signers and verifiers together. The domain-registry witness reads zero versioned tags and gains colon and spaced spelling fixtures; the evergreen version ceiling drops 58 → 55. The registry header names the re-key: a rename re-keys every record made under the old name, and no record crosses a rename (no backward compatibility in early alpha). The custody-root golden vector re-pins to the renamed domain (HKDF-SHA256 recomputed, matching CI).

Reads: Luna cold read LAND-AFTER-CURES, cures landed. Pre-push gate green; CI green at 9368a327f. Genesis format strings stay for the one labelled re-bake in the pre-rite.

